      "hints": [
        "Find $g^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x-1}{5}$.",
        "Substitute $f(x) = x + \\frac{1}{x}$ into $g^{-1}(x)$.",
        "Simplify $\\frac{x + 1/x - 1}{5}$ to $\\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{5x}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the inverse function $g^{-1}(x)$ for $g(x) = 5x + 1$:\n$$y = 5x + 1 \\implies x = \\frac{y - 1}{5} \\implies g^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 1}{5}$$",
        "Substitute $f(x) = x + \\frac{1}{x}$ into $g^{-1}(x)$:\n$$g^{-1}f(x) = \\frac{\\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right) - 1}{5}$$",
        "Combine the numerator into a single fraction and simplify:\n$$g^{-1}f(x) = \\frac{\\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{x}}{5} = \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{5x}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
